# Solidity source is fed straight into solc for compilation, and solc embeds a
# metadata hash of the exact source bytes into the compiled bytecode. Without
# this, a Windows checkout (CRLF, via core.autocrlf) and a Linux CI/container
# checkout (LF) of the identical commit compile to genuinely different
# bytecode, which breaks any byte-for-byte comparison against a hardcoded
# reference (see x/humanity/keeper/contract_deploy.go's V7ContractBytecode
# and its sync test). Force LF on disk everywhere so solc always sees the
# same bytes regardless of the checkout platform.
*.sol text eol=lf
